title:: BMAudioMatrix
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - routes signals on audio input busses to audio output busses
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMAudioMatrix is used to route audio signals from a set of input busses to a set of output busses. As such it can serve as a general purpose audio patch bay. These inputs and outputs are specified as instances of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::. 

See link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractMatrix:: for creation methods, etc.

See also: link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::, link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractAudioChainElement::, link::Classes/Matrices/BMAudioMixerMatrix::

Examples::

code::
// Audio matrix example
(
// make a speaker list
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

// something to route
(
b = Bus.audio(s, 8);
x = { Out.ar(b, {|i| Ringz.ar(Dust.ar(3, 0.1), 300 * (i + 1), 2)} ! 8) }.play;
)

// make a matrix
m = BMAudioMatrix(b.asBMInOutArray(\ringzes), l);

s.meter; // so we can watch

m.connect('ringzes-1', 'L');

m.connect('ringzes-2', 'L');

m.connect('ringzes-3', 'Ls', 'Rs');

m.disconnect('ringzes-1', 'L');

m.connect('ringzes-1', 'R');

m.mappings;

m.gui; // Use a GUI. Be sure to click 'View Matrix' for alternate view.

m.clear(3); // fade out connections

m.free; b.free; x.free;
::
